122-### §1 Command structure & naming
123-
124-**R1.1 — Noun-verb ordering. (MUST, Standard profile)**
125-A command path **MUST** read *resource then action*: `acme <noun> <verb>`. This is the de facto pattern of the most-praised multi-resource CLIs (gh, kubectl) and scales as resources grow.
126-✅ `acme project create`, `acme deploy list`
127-❌ `acme create project`, `acme list-deploys`
128-
129-**R1.2 — Nesting depth. (SHOULD)**
130-Subcommand depth after the binary **SHOULD NOT** exceed three path elements (`acme <group> <noun> <verb>`). Group nouns only when a flat noun set becomes unwieldy. Deeper nesting harms discoverability and tab-completion.
